<Base>
  <p class="eyebrow">Developer docs</p>
  <h1>Build on khensu.ñü</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    khensu.ñü is a post-quantum private messenger on a network run by people, and the first app on webË. These docs
    are for people who want to run part of the network, review the design, or contribute.
  </p>

  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Post-quantum everywhere.</b> Every message, call, payment and signature uses NIST’s post-quantum standards, ML-KEM-1024 and ML-DSA-87, inside the IETF’s Messaging Layer Security (MLS).</li>
    <li><b>Stealth is not optional.</b> Every message travels through a mix network, and every phone sends the same constant rhythm whether or not you’re using it. There is no setting to turn it off.</li>
    <li><b>Nothing is processed on servers.</b> Search, summaries and answers come from private AI on your own device. There are no AI nodes or servers for your data to leak to, and no iCloud or Siri.</li>
    <li><b>Run by people.</b> Nodes run on Raspberry Pi 5 boards, Macs, laptops and old phones in people’s homes, paid for the work they can prove they did.</li>
  </ul>

